---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
import Disclosure from '../../components/Disclosure.astro';
import EmailCapture from '../../components/EmailCapture.astro';
import { url } from '../../utils/url';
import { SITE } from '../../consts';
import { goHref, retailerName } from '../../data/affiliate-config';
import atoData from '../../data/atos.json';

interface ATO {
  brand: string; model: string; priceUSD: number; sensorType: string; sensorCount: number;
  failsafes: string[]; pumpMaxHeadFt: number | null; controllerTieIn: string;
  verifiedOn?: string; retailers?: string[]; source: string; imageUrl?: string | null;
}
const data = atoData as any;
// Ranked by layers of overfill protection first (the failure that matters), then price.
const atos = (data.atos as ATO[]).slice().sort(
  (a, b) => (b.failsafes.length - a.failsafes.length) || (a.priceUSD - b.priceUSD)
);
const dataDate = data.generated as string;

const slug = (a: { brand: string; model: string }) =>
  `${a.brand}-${a.model}`.toLowerCase().replace(/[^a-z0-9]+/g, '-').replace(/(^-|-$)/g, '');
const money = (n: number) => `$${n.toLocaleString('en-US', { minimumFractionDigits: 2, maximumFractionDigits: 2 })}`;
const buy = (a: ATO) => goHref(a.retailers || [], `${a.brand} ${a.model} auto top off`, a.source);
const byModel = (m: string) => (data.atos as ATO[]).find((a) => a.model.includes(m))!;

interface Pick { badge: string; why: string; a: ATO; }
const picks: Pick[] = [
  {
    badge: 'Mechanical float backup',
    why: `Dual optical sensing, a run-time cutoff, and a mechanical float valve provide several types of backup. Verify installation height and test the shutoffs before leaving it unattended.`,
    a: byModel('ATK v2'),
  },
  {
    badge: 'Optical + thermal backup',
    why: `The current Osmolator 3 pairs an optical water-level sensor with an independent thermal safety sensor. Its pump includes dry-run and blockage protection.`,
    a: byModel('Osmolator 3'),
  },
  {
    badge: 'Best value with a backup sensor',
    why: `Dual optical sensors and a learned-baseline alarm. Compare the backup behavior in the manual, and keep the reservoir size within a safe limit for your tank.`,
    a: byModel('Duetto2'),
  },
  {
    badge: 'Budget — single sensor',
    why: `One optical sensor, with the recorded QST cutoff and siphon break but no separate backup level sensor. Keep the reservoir limited and compare these safeguards with dual-sensor units.`,
    a: byModel('Smart ATO Micro'),
  },
];

const pageURL = new URL(url('/reviews/best-ato'), SITE.url).href;
const itemListLd = {
  '@context': 'https://schema.org',
  '@type': 'ItemList',
  name: 'Best Auto Top-Off (ATO) Systems for Reef Tanks',
  numberOfItems: atos.length,
  itemListElement: atos.map((a, i) => ({ '@type': 'ListItem', position: i + 1, name: `${a.brand} ${a.model}`, url: `${pageURL}#${slug(a)}` })),
};
const faqs = [
  {
    q: 'Do I actually need an ATO?',
    a: `An ATO is optional, but it can replace the freshwater lost to evaporation without repeated manual fills. Salt remains behind as water evaporates. Measure your own daily evaporation and check salinity rather than assuming a universal daily percentage.`,
  },
  {
    q: 'What actually fails on an ATO?',
    a: `The sensor, in the "on" position. A fouled or stuck sensor keeps the pump running, which pumps your entire freshwater reservoir into the tank — crashing salinity and often flooding the floor. That's why sensor count and failsafe layers are the first column in our ranking, not the pump specs. Calcium buildup, algae, and snails sitting on the sensor are the classic triggers; clean the sensor when you clean the glass.`,
  },
  {
    q: 'Optical or float sensor?',
    a: `Optical has no moving parts to jam with salt creep, which is why nearly every current unit leads with one. Some designs pair optical sensing with another method, such as the Osmolator 3 thermal sensor or the ATK mechanical float valve. Different methods add a backup; they do not guarantee against every fault.`,
  },
  {
    q: 'How big should the reservoir be?',
    a: `Measure your daily freshwater use, then choose a reservoir for the time between planned refills. Also consider what would happen if its whole contents reached the tank: extra freshwater lowers salinity and can overflow the system. Check the pump lift and anti-siphon instructions, and test the shutoffs with someone present.`,
  },
];
const faqLd = {
  '@context': 'https://schema.org',
  '@type': 'FAQPage',
  mainEntity: faqs.map((f) => ({ '@type': 'Question', name: f.q, acceptedAnswer: { '@type': 'Answer', text: f.a } })),
};

const headline = "Best ATO for a reef tank: auto top off with backups";
const quickPick = byModel('Osmolator 3');
---
<Base
  headline={headline}
  title="Best ATO for Reef Tanks: Auto Top Off (2026)"
  description="Compare reef auto top-off systems by overfill protection, sensor failsafes, and price. See Tunze, Neptune, XP Aqua, and other ATO options."
  breadcrumbs={[{ name: 'Reviews', href: '/reviews' }, { name: 'Best ATO Systems', href: '/reviews/best-ato' }]}
>
  <section class="container tool-wrap prose">
    <p class="eyebrow" style="color:var(--brand-2)">Reviews · Auto Top-Off</p>
    <h1>{headline}</h1>
    <p class="lede-dark">The best auto top off for a reef tank needs a backup if its main sensor stays on. The {quickPick.brand} {quickPick.model} is our starting pick for readers who want {quickPick.sensorType}: its recorded price is {money(quickPick.priceUSD)}. Compare pump lift, backup shutoffs, and reservoir size before choosing an ATO; extra sensors do not remove every failure risk.</p>
    <h2 id="quick-answer">Best ATO: what changes the choice?</h2>
    <p><strong>Different sensor technologies:</strong> compare the current Tunze Osmolator 3 optical and thermal sensors. <strong>A mechanical final stop:</strong> Neptune's ATK v2 includes a float valve as well as optical sensing. <strong>Lower recorded cost:</strong> compare XP Aqua and IceCap against the full protection list below. The table sorts recorded safeguard entries, then recorded price. Dry-run protection protects the pump; it is not an extra overfill sensor. This count does not measure reliability.</p>
    <p>Use freshwater for evaporation replacement: the salt stays in the aquarium. Keep the reservoir small enough to limit a stuck-on pump's impact, and verify the <a href={url('/tools/salinity-calculator')}>salinity reading</a> if the tank's water level changes unexpectedly. For a larger build, the <a href={url('/guides/120-gallon-reef-tank-setup')}>120-gallon setup guide</a> includes top-off storage in the plan.</p>
    <Disclosure />
    <p class="rnote" style="margin-top:0">Original dataset: {dataDate}. Tunze Osmolator 3 and 3 Nano models, specs, and prices were checked on October 25, 2026; other rows retain the older recorded prices. Follow each source to check the current listing. <a href={url('/how-we-rate')}>Full methodology →</a></p>
  </section>

  <section class="container" style="padding-top:8px;padding-bottom:16px;">
    <h2>The picks</h2>
    <div class="results">
      {picks.map((p, idx) => (
        <div id={`${slug(p.a)}-pick`} class={`rcard ${idx === 0 ? 'win' : ''}`}>
          {p.a.imageUrl && (
            <div class="rthumb">
              <img src={p.a.imageUrl} alt={`${p.a.brand} ${p.a.model}`} loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="64" height="64" onerror="this.parentElement.style.display='none'" />
            </div>
          )}
          <div class="rmain">
            <div class="rname">{p.a.brand} {p.a.model} <span class={idx === 0 ? 'pill-win' : 'rbadge'}>{p.badge}</span></div>
            <div class="rmeta">{p.why}</div>
            <div class="rmeta">{p.a.sensorType} · {p.a.controllerTieIn}</div>
          </div>
          <div class="rflow"><span class="n">{p.a.failsafes.length}</span><br /><span class="u">recorded safeguards</span></div>
          <div class="rbuy"><a class="aff" href={buy(p.a)} target="_blank" rel="sponsored nofollow noopener">{money(p.a.priceUSD)} at {retailerName(p.a.retailers)} (paid link) ↗</a></div>
        </div>
      ))}
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="container" style="padding-top:8px;">
    <h2>Every unit: sensors, safeguards, and pump lift</h2>
    <div class="tablewrap" tabindex="0" role="region" aria-label="Equipment comparison, scroll for all columns">
      <table class="specs">
        <thead><tr><th>#</th><th>ATO</th><th>Sensors</th><th>Failsafe layers</th><th>Pump lift / setup</th><th>Price</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
          {atos.map((a, i) => (
            <tr id={slug(a)}>
              <td>{i + 1}</td>
              <td><strong>{a.brand}</strong> {a.model}<br /><a href={a.source} target="_blank" rel="noopener">Listing and specs</a>{a.verifiedOn && <><br /><small>Checked {a.verifiedOn}</small></>}<br /><span style="color:var(--muted);font-size:.85em;">{a.sensorType}</span></td>
              <td>{a.sensorCount}</td>
              <td style="color:var(--muted)">{a.failsafes.join(' · ')}</td>
              <td style="color:var(--muted)">{a.pumpMaxHeadFt != null ? `${a.pumpMaxHeadFt} ft maximum lift` : 'Lift not recorded'} · {a.controllerTieIn}</td>
              <td><a class="aff aff-sm" href={buy(a)} target="_blank" rel="sponsored nofollow noopener">{money(a.priceUSD)} (paid link) ↗</a></td>
            </tr>
          ))}
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
    <p class="rnote">The safeguard list mixes level backups, timers, alarms, and pump protection. These perform different jobs, so a longer list does not prove a safer ATO. Confirm each shutoff in the manufacturer instructions, secure the tubing, and prevent a siphon. No failure-rate or service-life comparison is claimed.</p>
  </section>

  <section class="container prose" style="padding-top:24px;">
    <h2>FAQ</h2>
    <p>An ATO replaces evaporated fresh water; it does not replace salt lost during a water change. Use the <a href={url('/tools/salinity-calculator')}>salinity calculator</a> to understand your readings, and compare <a href={url('/reviews/best-reef-salt-mix')}>reef salt mixes</a> separately when planning new saltwater.</p>
    {faqs.map((f) => (
      <>
        <h3 style="font-size:1.05rem;">{f.q}</h3>
        <p style="color:var(--muted)">{f.a}</p>
      </>
    ))}
    <p>Planning the rest of the build? Evaporation scales with tank size — the setup guides cover where the ATO fits: <a href={url('/guides/75-gallon-reef-tank-setup')}>75 gallon</a> · <a href={url('/guides/120-gallon-reef-tank-setup')}>120 gallon</a>.</p>
  </section>

  <section class="container">
    <EmailCapture />
  </section>

  <script type="application/ld+json" set:html={JSON.stringify(itemListLd)} />
  <script type="application/ld+json" set:html={JSON.stringify(faqLd)} />
</Base>

<style>
  .tablewrap { overflow-x: auto; background: #fff; border: 1px solid var(--line); border-radius: var(--radius); box-shadow: var(--shadow); }
  table.specs { width: 100%; border-collapse: collapse; font-size: .92rem; min-width: 720px; }
  table.specs th { text-align: left; font-family: var(--font-display); font-size: .78rem; text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: .08em; color: var(--muted); padding: 12px 14px; border-bottom: 2px solid var(--line); }
  table.specs td { padding: 10px 14px; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line); vertical-align: top; }
  table.specs tr:last-child td { border-bottom: none; }
  .aff-sm { padding: 7px 12px; font-size: .8rem; }
</style>
